Write a Python module that turns a full patient transcript (list of turns,
see data/fixtures/sample_conversation_es.json for shape) into a structured
clinical intake record (see data/fixtures/sample_structured_intake.json for
the exact target shape).

Interface:

    build_intake(session_id: str, patient_ref: str, transcript: list[dict]) -> dict

Each transcript turn has: turn (int), speaker ("agent"|"patient"), ts (str),
text (str, Spanish).

For every clinical field extracted (chief_complaint, onset, duration,
severity_0_10, associated_symptoms, current_medications, allergies,
relevant_history), the output entry must include:
    value               translated to English (use translator.translate_turn)
    source_span         the exact original Spanish substring that supports it
    source_turn         the turn number it came from
    stated_by_patient    false if the field was inferred rather than stated
                         directly (e.g. a condition inferred from a
                         medication's indication) — set a "note" explaining
                         the inference in that case

Detect red flags (e.g. chest pain radiating to the arm, shortness of breath,
sudden/acute onset) and set triage_priority to one of "ROUTINE", "URGENT",
"EMERGENT", plus a red_flags list of short strings.

Produce english_summary: a one-paragraph clinician-facing summary of the
whole encounter.

Never fabricate a field that has no supporting turn — omit it instead of
guessing. Raise PipelineError if transcript is empty.
